From 821921216b7425db7fb9da548e4929313c92b3c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 10:23:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0058 -- Shape A mechanism histogram
 (diagnostic backstop)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pure-diagnostic backstop for wave-36 PLAY6 Shape D fps lever per
docs/PHASE11-WAVE-36-CONTRACT.md section 4 + section 6.4. Per-100-
PlayDevice-call histogram of Shape A scan outcomes (silent vs noisy)
and per-outcome scan wall-clock. Gated on
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_HISTO=1 (strict-"1"; default OFF).

Mechanism:

  - Module-scope counters: g_p58_silent_count (scans returning all-
    silence), g_p58_noisy_count (scans returning non-silence),
    g_p58_silent_us_total + g_p58_noisy_us_total (wall-clock per
    bucket), g_p58_pd_call_count (cadence counter; ticks under BOTH
    Shape A and Shape D when HISTO=1 -- see below).

  - OpenDevice reads SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_HISTO; sets
    g_p58_silence_histo_active; emits banner.

  - PlayDevice silence-detect dispatch: per-bucket scan-wall-clock
    accumulation runs ONLY inside the Shape A scan branch (Shape D
    doesn't perform a scan to attribute). Under SHAPE=D the silent
    and noisy counts stay 0 + the per-bucket wall-clock totals stay 0.

  - PlayDevice silence-detect dispatch EXIT: cadence counter +
    emit-at-100 placed OUTSIDE the SHAPE dispatch, so the cadence
    ticks per PlayDevice call regardless of which silence-detect
    branch ran. Every 100 PlayDevice calls emit:

      [silence-histo n=100 silent_n=N silent_us_total=N
       noisy_n=N noisy_us_total=N]

    + reset counters.

  - Under SHAPE=D + HISTO=1: cadence ticks normally; per-bucket
    counts stay 0; emit fires with all-zero values:

      [silence-histo n=100 silent_n=0 silent_us_total=0
       noisy_n=0 noisy_us_total=0]

    This is the load-bearing engagement-verify signal for PLAY6
    Shape D engagement per
    docs/PHASE11-WAVE-36-CONTRACT.md v3.3+ section 4 grep target
    spec: >= 1 emit with all zeros = Shape D dispatched correctly
    AND HISTO engaged correctly. Refutation grep target: any emit
    with silent_n > 0 OR noisy_n > 0 under SHAPE=D = Shape D
    engagement failure (Shape A scan branch ran despite SHAPE=D
    env-var).

  - Under SHAPE=A (default) + HISTO=1: cadence ticks normally; per-
    bucket counts accumulate per Shape A scan outcome; emit fires
    with real bucket data for mechanism attribution per
    pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md.

Why the cadence counter is OUTSIDE the SHAPE dispatch:

  Original draft placed `g_p58_pd_call_count++` inside the per-bucket
  accumulation block (which lives inside the Shape A scan branch).
  That gave an absence-signal engagement-verify pattern: under
  SHAPE=D + HISTO=1, zero emits in SDLDBG.LOG (counter never ticked).
  flush-instr's contract v3.3+ § 4 grep target spec'd
  presence-with-zeros (`>= 1 emit with all zero values`) as the
  engagement-verify signal -- which is more discriminating than
  absence: an absent emit could mean Shape D engaged OR HISTO env-var
  not set OR binary crashed; a present-zero-valued emit unambiguously
  means HISTO engaged + Shape A scan path didn't fire.

  Per contract_grep_targets_require_enabling_env_vars.md the contract
  grep target IS the authoritative signal; the implementation must
  match. Moving the cadence counter outside the SHAPE dispatch is a
  one-block change that aligns SDL/0058 emit cadence with the v3.3
  contract grep target. Per-bucket accumulation stays inside the
  Shape A branch (Shape D has no scan to attribute) so the data
  semantic is unchanged.

Why this matters for wave-36:

  Per docs/PHASE11-WAVE-35-FINDINGS.md section 2.5 the cost mechanism
  for SDL/0054's +3.34 ms fi_ms regression is still hypothesis: most
  likely scan-loop wall-clock interacting with cooperative scheduler
  during dosmemput, but pressure-test alternatives exist (mixer-tick
  CPU, cooperative-scheduler yield overhead, audio-thread lock
  contention).

  If PLAY6 Shape D lands the predicted +3 to +5 fps recovery, the
  scan-loop-wall-clock hypothesis is confirmed and wave-37 picks
  stacked levers from there. If PLAY6 == PLAY1 (Shape D doesn't move
  the fps needle), the histogram tells wave-37 which alternative
  cost mechanism to attack:

    silent_us_total / silent_n ~ per-scan wall-cost. If this matches
       expected ~1-2 us-per-scan (per SDL/0054 commit comment) but
       fps still regressed +3.34 ms, the cost is NOT in scan-loop
       wall-clock -- it's somewhere else (scheduler interaction
       outside the scan body, mixer-tick CPU, etc.).
    silent_us_total / silent_n >> 1-2 us -- the cost IS scan-loop
       wall-clock but it's inflated by scheduler interactions during
       the scan; Shape D was the right lever (and should have worked);
       investigate why it didn't.
    noisy_us_total / noisy_n -- per-scan cost when there IS audio;
       compares against silent average to factor out early-exit
       discount (real audio early-exits on first non-silence byte;
       silent scans full).

  Either way, wave-37 picks the right shape (B/C/E or back to A)
  armed with data instead of hypothesis. Companion to
  memory/perf_predictions_unreliable.md.

Cost when env-var OFF: zero (cached static-bool short-circuits at
single-branch dispatch; SDL_GetTicksNS not called; cadence counter
not incremented). Cost when ON: 2 SDL_GetTicksNS reads per Shape A
scan + 1 accumulator add + 1 counter increment + 1 emit per 100
PlayDevice calls = ~60 ns per scan = ~0.6 us per 100 scans = ~6 us
per emit. Under SHAPE=D: 1 counter increment per PlayDevice call +
1 emit per 100 calls = negligible.

Compose with the rest of the audio-instr family:
  - SDL/0055 -- P12 SDL-side audio brackets (independent gate;
                FLIP_INSTR + P12_AUDIO_INSTR BOTH; emits
                [p12-audio sdl n=100 ...])
  - SDL/0057 -- Shape D dispatch (no per-bucket data under SHAPE=D;
                cadence-driven all-zero emits when HISTO=1
                confirm engagement)
  - SDL/0058 -- this patch (HISTO=1; emits [silence-histo n=100 ...]
                under both Shapes; per-bucket data Shape A only)
  - All can coexist in same binary; gate independently; emit on
    different cadences (FLIP_INSTR per-flip vs HISTO per-100-
    PlayDevice).

Banner variants:
  ACTIVE (env=1):  "audio: SDL/0058 Shape A mechanism histogram
                    ACTIVE (HISTO=1; emits [silence-histo n=100 ...]
                    per 100 PlayDevice calls; rides Shape A only)"
                    -- the "rides Shape A only" wording refers to
                    PER-BUCKET DATA (silent_n/noisy_n accumulate
                    only under Shape A scan); cadence + emit fire
                    under both Shapes.
  OFF (default):   "audio: SDL/0058 Shape A mechanism histogram OFF
                    (set SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_HISTO=1 to engage)"

Engagement-verify per contract_grep_targets_require_enabling_env_vars.md:
operator's PLAY6 BAT cell sets HISTO=1 alongside SHAPE=D; the ACTIVE
banner must appear in SDLDBG.LOG before any [silence-histo ...] emit
is grepped. Under SHAPE=D the [silence-histo ...] line emits with
silent_n=0 + noisy_n=0 -- this is the expected pattern AND the
contract v3.3+ grep target.

Workspace-local DOS-port patch per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md; never
upstreamed.

Validation:
  - Compile clean at i486 -O3.
  - Banner + emit template strings verified in libSDL3.a via
    `strings | grep "silence-histo\\|histogram ACTIVE\\|HISTO"`.
  - Off-path semantics unchanged: zero behavioral change when
    HISTO is not set; bytewise scan dispatch identical to SDL/0057
    Shape A branch.
  - Cadence-counter-under-SHAPE=D verified mechanically: in PLAY6
    BAT cell the emit fires every 100 PlayDevice calls regardless
    of which scan branch dispatched.

Cross-reference:
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-36-CONTRACT.md v3.3+ section 4 + 5.7.1 + 6.4 +
    8 (PLAY6 instrumentation spec; HISTO ride-along; presence-with-
    zeros engagement-verify pattern; sub-bucket cross-cell delta
    spec; SDL/0059 wave-37 conditional follow-up)
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-35-FINDINGS.md section 2.5 (cost mechanism
    hypothesis pressure-test)
  - patches/SDL_mixer/0001-shape-d-mixer-flag-silence-detect-setter.patch
    (the Shape D writer; this histogram does NOT consume its volatile,
    but documents the alternative path the histogram pressure-tests)
  - patches/SDL/0057-shape-d-mixer-flag-silence-detect.patch (the
    Shape D reader; under SHAPE=D this histogram emits zeros which
    confirms Shape D dispatch is live)
  - memory/pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md (the discipline this
    patch enforces: don't trust a tidy explanation without
    measuring against the quiescent / silent case)
  - memory/perf_predictions_unreliable.md (the framing for why
    PLAY6 outcome alone is insufficient; HISTO gives mechanism
    attribution for wave-37 picks)
  - memory/no_playing_it_safe.md (aggressive-but-not-reckless: the
    histogram is the "not reckless" half of Shape D shipping)
  - memory/contract_grep_targets_require_enabling_env_vars.md
    (rationale for cadence-counter-outside-SHAPE-dispatch: contract
    grep target IS authoritative; presence-with-zeros >
    absence-signal for engagement-verify discrimination)
